    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67858" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῑμ-ητής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>imitator</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινων</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.6.3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Vict.</u>
				1.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Cor.</u>
				4.16
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ μ. τῶν γραμμάτων</span>
			<i>forgers</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				115.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>artist</i> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίμησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				602a
			</span></i>, al.; esp. <i>one who impersonates</i> characters, as an
			actor or poet, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				918b28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Po.</u>
				1460a8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> coupled with
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γόης</span>, <i>mere actor,
			impostor</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				598d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Plt.</u>
				303c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sph.</u>
				235a
			</span></i>.</div>
